  "hypothesis": "A bounded insertion sort for buckets of at most eight indices may avoid qsort overhead on tiny buckets, while retaining qsort for larger buckets to preserve scalable lexicographic sorting.",
  "notes": "The insertion-sort work is capped at eight elements. No SIMD directive is added because bucket-counter and scatter updates have write dependencies.",
